00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:35.880
and set the next opportunity for 12.5 PM Eastern on Thursday, November 19th.

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:43.380
The spacecraft is returning more than 6,300 pounds of cargo, including 3D bioprinted blood vessel constructs,

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:48.580
frozen tumor organoids, which are lab-grown tumor samples, and microbial samples.

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:53.140
A lighting system that spent more than three years on the station is coming home, too,

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:57.600
after tests of whether it can help astronaut sleep and stay well on long missions.

00:00:57.600 --> 00:00:57.760
actions.

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:03.500
That dragon arrived at the station on October 15 after launching two days earlier on a Falcon

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:06.880
9 from Space Launch Complex 40 at Cape Canaveral.

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:13.460
Mission teams will hold the next weather review at 12 p.m. eastern on November 18, before confirming

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:14.420
the Thursday window.

00:01:15.488 --> 00:01:21.568
Elon Musk in remarks reported by Yahoo Finance said ship 42 could probably be reflown with

00:01:21.568 --> 00:01:25.048
a few weeks of refurbishment after he inspected the heat shield himself.

00:01:25.048 --> 00:01:31.388
That upper stage put 26 Starlink version 3 satellites into orbit on one flight, a load

00:01:31.388 --> 00:01:34.868
that would take roughly 10 Falcon 9 launches with older satellites.

00:01:35.468 --> 00:01:40.608
Falcon 9 and Falcon Heavy cannot fly the version 3 satellites, so scaling that part of the

00:01:40.608 --> 00:01:44.888
constellation without building a new upper stage every time depends on flying recovered

00:01:44.888 --> 00:01:45.548
starships.

00:01:46.148 --> 00:01:51.628
SpaceX has already reflown two super heavy boosters, the first stage of the stack, the first

00:01:51.628 --> 00:01:56.828
after four months and the second after seven months. Musk noted that Starship still requires

00:01:56.828 --> 00:02:01.888
several fixes before it can fly like an airplane with only scheduled maintenance between flights.

00:02:02.428 --> 00:02:08.108
SpaceX has targeted early 2027 for the first flight of a recovered Starship upper stage.

00:02:08.957 --> 00:02:14.357
The United Kingdom now has access the UK Defense Journal reports to a considerable number

00:02:14.357 --> 00:02:19.297
of Starshield terminals for defense use. Starshield is the government version of Starlink,

00:02:19.297 --> 00:02:22.557
built as military-grade hardware for official customers.

00:02:23.077 --> 00:02:27.977
The terminals provide secure communications links that run on their own capacity, separate

00:02:27.977 --> 00:02:29.617
from the commercial star-link network.

00:02:30.623 --> 00:02:37.143
An air permit, according to MLQ for SpaceX's 750-megawatt gas plant at Starbase, was approved

00:02:37.143 --> 00:02:37.803
by Texas.

00:02:38.563 --> 00:02:43.663
The permit covers construction and operation of the gas-fired power facility, intended to

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:46.623
support expanded operations at the Texas launch site.

00:02:46.623 --> 00:02:51.323
data center permit processing in the region has also restarted after earlier

00:02:51.323 --> 00:02:56.043
pauses. The combined infrastructure supports both launch cadence and on-site

00:02:56.043 --> 00:03:02.242
compute growth. In the same window, Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky stated in

00:03:02.242 --> 00:03:06.542
remarks reported by Tokenpost that speed restrictions on star shield in

00:03:06.542 --> 00:03:10.702
temporarily occupied territories remain in place while discussions continue with

00:03:10.702 --> 00:03:15.782
the United States side. Rocket Lab completed its 100th electron mission on November

00:03:15.782 --> 00:03:21.562
14th NASA Space Flight Reports, becoming the fastest commercially developed rocket to hit

00:03:21.562 --> 00:03:28.042
that milestone, with a $3.57 billion backlog of contract admissions, carrying the Yamat

00:03:28.042 --> 00:03:34.062
Sumi 2 satellite for IQPS, a synthetic aperture radar that builds images from radio echoes,

00:03:34.622 --> 00:03:39.722
from launch Complex 1 in New Zealand. Elon Musk posted that Starship has the mandate

00:03:39.722 --> 00:03:45.062
of heaven, while emphasizing he does not want to be king. He also said roughly a megaton

00:03:45.062 --> 00:03:49.862
of mass per year to orbit is required to build self-sustaining cities on the moon and Mars.

00:03:50.622 --> 00:03:54.702
Worth keeping an eye on, star-shield speed limits and occupied Ukrainian areas,

00:03:55.262 --> 00:04:00.762
MLQ notes, can disrupt service for Ukrainian drones traveling around 100 miles per hour or

00:04:00.762 --> 00:04:06.428
faster. The limits are set by the United States government, which controls the military grade

00:04:06.428 --> 00:04:11.628
constellation. Resolving the issue would require changes in United States policy on terminal

00:04:11.628 --> 00:04:17.008
performance in the region. For the Starship Upper Stage Musk walked, the engineering reality

00:04:17.008 --> 00:04:21.908
sits in the heat shield tiles, not in the catch hardware. Each tile has to live through

00:04:21.908 --> 00:04:26.228
the hottest stretch of reentry and still stay bonded while the air stream loads and shakes

00:04:26.228 --> 00:04:31.688
the vehicle. Because a lost bond lets hot plasma reach the structure behind it. Heating

00:04:31.688 --> 00:04:36.548
is the energy the tile must refuse. Dynamic pressure is the force of the airflow trying

00:04:36.548 --> 00:04:40.288
to peel it off, and those are two different ways the same array can fail.

00:04:40.848 --> 00:04:45.708
When the tiles come through intact, groundwork shrinks to spot checks, a little sealant

00:04:45.708 --> 00:04:50.228
and a sign-off on the thermal protection system, instead of pulling the array and building

00:04:50.228 --> 00:04:50.688
it again.

00:04:51.368 --> 00:04:58.048
Ship 42 completed 14 orbits on Flight 15, and spent 22.5 hours in space before the tower

00:04:58.048 --> 00:05:03.548
caught the Starship upper stage, giving engineers flight data on those tiles under real reentry

00:05:03.548 --> 00:05:03.968
heating.

00:05:03.968 --> 00:05:11.068
Canetic energy is 1.5 mass times velocity squared, so at roughly 7.8 kilometers per second,

00:05:11.508 --> 00:05:15.968
that is on the order of 30 megajoules per kilogram the shield must keep out of the structure.

00:05:16.548 --> 00:05:19.308
That load is why a missing tile is not cosmetic.

00:05:19.848 --> 00:05:24.308
It is a hole in the only system standing between orbital speed and the vehicle underneath.

00:05:25.008 --> 00:05:30.128
An intact array decides the cost, because the dominant bill on an expendable upper stage

00:05:30.128 --> 00:05:35.128
is fabricating the structure and the propulsion system once, and that bill is paid again on

00:05:35.128 --> 00:05:37.308
every flight if the vehicle is thrown away.

00:05:37.908 --> 00:05:42.848
Fly the same ship and each extra kilogram to orbit is mostly propellant and range time,

00:05:43.388 --> 00:05:48.168
and the idiot index how many times the finished stage costs over the raw metal and propellant

00:05:48.168 --> 00:05:51.448
falls once you stop buying a new vehicle for each payload.

00:05:52.128 --> 00:05:56.328
Kitten procedures on the ground are scaled to flow a flown upper stage through inspection

00:05:56.328 --> 00:05:58.268
and out again without new facilities.

00:05:58.268 --> 00:06:03.428
repeat that cycle and upper-stage reuse stops being a structural rebuild and

00:06:03.428 --> 00:06:07.048
becomes a question of how fast you can load propellant and mate the payload.

00:06:07.528 --> 00:06:11.368
Whether the next recovered ship can match that inspection flow without extra

00:06:11.368 --> 00:06:16.128
tile work or swapping the flight computers is the next data point. That covers

00:06:16.128 --> 00:06:24.988
everything worth knowing about SpaceX today. SPCX closed at $141.70, up 3.2%.

